{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 10, 26]], "date-time": "2025-10-26T12:52:05Z", "timestamp": 1761483125684, "version": "build-2065373602"}, "reference-count": 111, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "3", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 9]], "date-time": "2025-07-09T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1752019200000}, "content-version": "am", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, {"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 9]], "date-time": "2025-07-09T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1752019200000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/100007917", "name": "Agricultural Research Service", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["5442\u20102030\u201021430\u2010015\u201000D", "5442\u201022000\u2010080\u2010037\u201000D", "FY18\u2010SP\u2010005"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["5442\u20102030\u201021430\u2010015\u201000D", "5442\u201022000\u2010080\u2010037\u201000D", "FY18\u2010SP\u2010005"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100007917", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["acsess.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["The Plant Genome"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Fusarium head blight (FHB), caused by\n                    <jats:italic>Fusarium graminearum</jats:italic>\n                    Schwabe, is one of the most devastating diseases in wheat (\n                    <jats:italic>Triticum aestivum</jats:italic>\n                    L.). The synthetic hexaploid wheat line Largo was developed from a cross between the durum wheat [\n                    <jats:italic>T. turgidum</jats:italic>\n                    ssp.\n                    <jats:italic>durum</jats:italic>\n                    (Desf.) Husn.] variety Langdon and the\n                    <jats:italic>Aegilops tauschii</jats:italic>\n                    Cosson accession PI 268210, and it was previously found to have a moderate level of FHB resistance. This study was conducted to identify quantitative trait loci (QTL) associated with FHB resistance using a population of 188 recombinant inbred lines (RILs) from a cross between Largo and the susceptible wheat line ND495. The RILs were evaluated for Type II resistance in two greenhouse and two field environments. The disease severity and 90K single\u2010nucleotide polymorphism marker data were used for QTL analysis, which revealed six QTL on chromosomes 1D, 2D, 5B, and 7D. Four QTL (\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20101D</jats:italic>\n                    ,\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20105B</jats:italic>\n                    ,\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20107D.1</jats:italic>\n                    , and\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20107D.3</jats:italic>\n                    ) from Largo had minor effects, whereas two QTL (\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20102D</jats:italic>\n                    and\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg</jats:italic>\n                    <jats:italic>\u20107D.2</jats:italic>\n                    ) from ND495 showed large effects on FHB resistance. The result suggested that ND495 may possess suppressor or susceptibility gene(s) suppressing or masking FHB resistance controlled by the resistance QTL. Among these QTL, four coincided with previously reported QTL, including\n                    <jats:italic>Fhb9</jats:italic>\n                    , and two (\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20101D</jats:italic>\n                    and\n                    <jats:italic>QFhb.rwg\u20107D.1</jats:italic>\n                    ) are likely novel QTL. From the six QTL regions, 10 Kompetitive allele\u2010specific PCR markers were developed and validated for marker\u2010assisted selection. The QTL detected from the resistant and susceptible parents enhance our understanding of FHB resistance expression and provide new resources for improving FHB resistance in wheat.\n                  </jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1002/tpg2.70073", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 10]], "date-time": "2025-07-10T05:23:40Z", "timestamp": 1752125020000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Identification and mapping of quantitative trait loci for Fusarium head blight resistance in a synthetic hexaploid \u00d7 hard red spring wheat population"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "18", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3392-6646", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Agnes", "family": "Szabo\u2010Hever", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "USDA\u2010ARS, Cereal Crops Improvement Research Unit, Edward T. Schafer Agricultural Research Center  Fargo North Dakota USA"}, {"name": "Department of Plant Sciences North Dakota State University  Fargo North Dakota USA"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5941-5548", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Jyoti S.", "family": "Sharma", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Plant Sciences North Dakota State University  Fargo North Dakota USA"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9653-3287", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Justin D.", "family": "Faris", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "USDA\u2010ARS, Cereal Crops Improvement Research Unit, Edward T. Schafer Agricultural Research Center  Fargo North Dakota USA"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1928-0877", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Shaobin", "family": "Zhong", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"nam